NVIC - Nested Vectored Interrupt Controller
   - The NVIC is a hardware block inside the ARM Cortex-M4 core that manages interrupts: enabling them, assigning priorities, tracking
     their status, and supporting interrupt nesting.
     
     1. Enablie and Disable IRQ
     	
     	#include "stm32f4xx.h"
     	
     	void interrupt_init(void)
     	{
     		NVIC_EnableIRQ(EXTI0_IRQn); // Enable EXTI0 Interrupt
     	}
     	
     	void interrupt_stop(void)
     	{
     		NVIC_DisableIRQ(EXTIO_IRQn); // Disable EXTI0 Interrupt
     	}
     	
     2. Interrupt Priority
     	a. Priority 0 : Highest Urgency
     	b. Priority 15: Lowest Urgency
     	
     	- A higher-priority interrupt can preempt a lower-priority ISR.
     	
     	
     	Example:
     	
     	void interrupt_init(void)
     	{
     		NVIC_SetPriority(EXTI0_IRQn, 2); // High Priority
     		NVIC_SetPriority(EXTI1_IRQn, 6); // Lower Priority
     		
     		NVIC_EnableIRQ(EXTI0_IRQn);
     		NVIC_EnableIRQ(EXTI1_IRQn);
     	}